     CDS             complement(871496..872089)
                     /locus_tag="FTT_0861c"
                     /note="Similar to FMA2_BACNO (P17824) Fimbrial protein
                     precursor (Pilin) from Bacteroides nodosus (Dichelobacter
                     nodosus) (160 aa). FASTA: opt: 169 Z-score: 222.1 E():
                     0.00018 Smith-Waterman score: 169; 34.646 identity in 127
                     aa overlap The pili fiber building block protein has a
                     highly distinct primary structure; a short positively
                     charged leader sequence, and a highly conserved and highly
                     hydrophobic amino-terminal domain which forms the core of
                     the pilus fiber; A variety of studies suggest that the
                     invariant glycine (G) at -1 is required for prepilin
                     cleavage and assembly and that the glutamate (E) at + 5 is
                     essential for assembly and efficient N-terminal
                     methylation but not cleavage. The region near the carboxy
                     terminus is often hydrophilic and is stabilized by one or
                     two disulfide bridges that may be involved in recognition
                     of receptors. The genes with these characteristics are
                     usually termed pilA, pilE, pilV, pilW, pilX and FimU.
                     (Mattick John S.. 'Type IV Pili and twitching motility'.
                     Annu. Rev. Microbiol. 2002. 56:289-314.) This protein has
                     all the characteristics described above, but shows a weak
                     global homology. ORF ftt0861c"
